   Vacation Mail             
   ------------------------------------------------------------------------
   What is vacation mail?  It is the ability to tell the mail door that you
   will be away  for the next couple of days,  and ask it to pack your mail  
   for you automatically at night.  When you come back, you simply download
   each packet that was created for you, and turn off your vacation status.
   Each packet is exactly like if you had  downloaded it yourself each day,
   except you'll have a lot of reading to catch up on.

   Try to not leave the mail status on for too long, since it takes system 
   resources to pack and store your mail packets.    Generally, if you are 
   going to be away for an extreamly extended time,  you probably will not
   read all of the mail that was saved for you,  so in those cases try not
   use the vacation mail - if needed,  just select  those REALLY important
   areas that you can't miss...  perhaps only messages addressed to you?

   If you have any more questions just ask your Sysop.

 
